  "SUBJECTS_liquid_containers_four_styles": {
   "label": "Liquid containers, four styles",
   "slug": "liquid_containers_four_styles",
   "subjects": true,
   "ground_terrain": "Soil",
   "title": "Liquid containers, four styles \u2014 game art",
   "lead_html": "<p><b>Liquid containers, four styles</b> (LIQUID_CONTAINERS_REDRAW_NO_MANA_POTIONS). Owner 2026-10-16: <i>\u201cThe art for buckets, barrels, etc. is really boring. They too should have the four styles of art. And the bottles look like mana potions in fantasy games. This is a scifi future world. Junker bottles should be oddly shapes. Industrial should look like generic water bottles. Modern should look like soda bottles (multicolored). Futuristic should look like hexagonal canteens.\u201d</i></p>\n<p>One row per container \u00d7 style (Junker = our \u201cscrapper\u201d style). Each row is ONE sprite: the first column is the file that would install (the liquid drawn neutral grey); the other three are the same file with the liquid tinted fresh water / toxic water / tar, the way the game would tint it from a mask. So pick or note per ROW: keep, or what to change. Nothing is installed or wired yet; design: design/RimMandrake/liquid_containers_four_styles_2026-10-16.md.</p>\n",
